# Knowledge Graph Plan

The file `PLAN-knowledge-graph.md` in the project root is the implementation plan. Read it before starting work on any graph-related feature.

## Key architecture decisions

- Graph data lives in `.stack-compass/graph.db` (SQLite via `better-sqlite3` — required for FTS5)
- Existing 15 MCP tools and `ScannedModule` in-memory flow are unchanged — the graph is additive
- Cross-language linking uses convention-based string matching (operation names, URL paths, type names) — not type-system resolution
- Edge resolution runs as a second pass after all modules are ingested

## Recommended build order

1 → 3A → 2A → 3B → 2B → 4 → 5/6

1. SQLite storage (`src/graph/`)
2A. Same-language edges (`src/graph/resolvers/`)
2B. Cross-language edges (TS→GQL→Spring)
3A. Graph query tools (search-symbols, get-symbol-detail, graph-status)
3B. Graph traversal tools (get-callers, get-callees, get-impact, build-context)
4. Incremental sync
5. Google ADK support
6. Test impact analysis
